  "summary": {
    "as": "Introduced in House",
    "asOf": "2026-01-30",
    "date": "2026-09-17T15:42:27Z",
    "text": "AI for Secure Networks Act\n\nThis bill requires the National Telecommunications and Information Administration (NTIA) to study and report to Congress on the impact of artificial intelligence (AI) technology on the security of telecommunications networks.\n\nThe report must include an analysis of (1) how AI may be used to improve and increase the security of telecommunications networks, including in connection with Open Radio Access Network or virtualized security technologies; and (2) risks to telecommunications network security posed by AI. The\u00a0NTIA must seek public comment on the report before finalizing it and submitting it to Congress."
  },
